":"","img":"https://cdn.mycoast.photos/2025/08/15144525/9efa0f1a1bedee6e96827d91150244b5-scaled.jpg","depth":null,"flooded":"Sidewalks","rain24":0.021}},{"type":"Feature","geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-73.929467,40.757028]},"properties":{"id":209059,"url":"https://mycoast.org/reports/209059","date":"2025-07-14","place":"36th Ave N/W MTA stop","hood":"Astoria","boro":"Queens","text":"","img":"https://cdn.mycoast.photos/2025/07/16133708/0ad5554e17e254f2a743525b66a049448f118fca.jpg","depth":1,"flooded":"Roads/streets, Sidewalks, Other","rain24":0.039}},{"type":"Feature","geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-73.857939,40.669159]},"properties":{"id":204834,"url":"https://mycoast.org/reports/204834","date":"2025-06-02","place":"East New York, Kings County, NY","hood":"East New York","boro":"Brooklyn","text":"Estimated water depth: 2-8in. This photo was taken at the corner of Amber St and Loring Ave in East NY. This street is disconnected from NYC's municipal storm water system relying on cesspools for sewage storage that often overflow polluting the area. (This area is also known as the South Jewel Streets). This road ponding was still present after more than 24 hours without any precipitation and on a sunny 68ºF day. The street was impassible for cars who opted to skirt the narrow sidewalk pavement with the passenger side of the vehicles dipping slightly into the water instead of plowing through the large puddle. There was not enough space for both pedestrians and vehicles to pass each other. The road conditions are not ideal with many potholes and cracked pavement present as well as litter strewn and intermixed with mud and the partially paved, uneven street. There is not a dedicated sidewalk on the east side of the street separated from the traffic lane as well as on the west side. Cars park perpendicularly to the narrow walkway on the west side of Amber Street. The west side of the street's topography slopes upwards slightly and the north end at the junction with Linden Blvd (NY rt 27) rises up sharply to sea level with the rest of the street grid.","img":"https://cdn.mycoast.photos/2025/06/13011855/89f3c8800f329ca40921a95c1e2eceb94-scaled.jpg","depth":null,"flooded":"Roads/streets, Sidewalks, Lawns/vegetation","rain24":0}},{"type":"Feature","geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-73.856976,40.669106]},"properties":{"id":204841,"url":"https://mycoast.org/reports/204841","date":"2025-06-02","place":"Lindenwood, Queens County, NY","hood":"Howard Beach","boro":"Queens","text":"Estimated water depth: 2-5in. These photos were taken just one block east from my previous report at Amber St and Loring Av, at Loring Av and Sapphire St. Sapphire St alike Amber St is below sea level and does not have dedicated, separated sidewalks. (Sapphire has a gravel path that narrows significantly with street ponding). After crossing Linden Blvd(NY rt 27), Sapphire St slopes downwards sharply. Sapphire St is a mix of gravel, dirt and asphalt which also becomes muddy after rainfall. The roads are uneven, pot hole laden and cracked. (This area is along the Brooklyn Queens border of East NY and Lindenwood  and is also known as the South Jewel Streets). DSCF8744 shows the flooding conditions on Amber St compared to the other photos taken on Sapphire St. (These were taken at the same time).","img":"https://cdn.mycoast.photos/2025/06/13014217/73704370c58a1e132be01e418289fd994-scaled.jpg","depth":null,"flooded":"Roads/streets, Sidewalks, Lawns/vegetation","rain24":0}},{"type":"Feature","geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-73.859487,40.671467]},"properties":{"id":204850,"url":"https://mycoast.org/reports/204850","date":"2025-06-02","place":"The Hole (Lindenwood), Queens County, NY","hood":"Howard Beach","boro":"Queens","text":"Estimated water depth: 2-3in. The Hole is disconnected from NYC's municipal stormwater sewage system (bordered by Conduit and Linden Blvds to the northeast and south and Drew St to the west). It is below sea level and the roads are partially paved, mostly dirt mixed with asphalt, full of pot holes, cracks and awfully muddy. There is minimal drainage to the area with one catch basin installed by the NYCDEP at 77th St and Dumont Ave 1 block east of the puddles on 76th St. DSCF8744 shows flooding one block north at 76th St and Blake Avenue. This flooding was on a sunny 68ºF day just north of Linden Blvd (NY rt 27) and my two other companion flood reports from Sapphire and Amber Streets.","img":"https://cdn.mycoast.photos/2025/06/13021524/6c7722a19b798bce6024e83eddb95d554-scaled.jpg","depth":2,"flooded":"Roads/streets, Sidewalks","rain24":0}},{"type":"Feature","geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-73.823172,40.583663]},"properties":{"id":201277,"url":"https://mycoast.org/reports/201277","date":"2025-05-05","place":"","hood":"Seaside","boro":"Queens","text":"","img":"https://cdn.mycoast.photos/2025/05/05192558/52a6134f9b63ccbfcc59fe80a97723a7035c277b.jpg","depth":1,"flooded":"Roads/streets","rain24":0.932}},{"type":"Feature","geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-73.795861,40.806911]},"properties":{"id":201185,"url":"https://mycoast.org/reports/201185","date":"2025-05-05","place":"SUNY maritime college","hood":"East Bronx","boro":"Bronx","text":"","img":"https://cdn.mycoast.photos/2025/05/05151643/7f83f1b9ed1579fe650688f80f030c9f44196cf7.jpg","depth":2,"flooded":"Sidewalks","rain24":0.388}},{"type":"Feature","geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-73.795065,40.807924]},"properties":{"id":201518,"url":"https://mycoast.org/reports/201518","date":"2025-05-05","place":"SUNY Maritime (Erben Avenue)","hood":"East Bronx","boro":"Bronx","text":"","img":"https://cdn.mycoast.photos/2025/05/09120552/ea709b6712cc7434659f14fd4cf9f82abfe319f3.jpg","depth":3,"flooded":"Roads/streets","rain24":0.19}},{"type":"Feature","geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-73.797855,40.808178]},"properties":{"id":198301,"url":"https://mycoast.org/reports/198301","date":"2025-03-24","place":"Pen