12', that's just a best guess for the deepest area as I didn't venture closer to the bay without waders.","img":"https://cdn.mycoast.photos/2024/06/01190709/6db8f47214c12332d80c620240d47efa0985c5b0-scaled.jpg","depth":12,"flooded":"Roads/streets, Sidewalks, Parking lots, Lawns/vegetation","rain24":0.075}},{"type":"Feature","geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-73.801269,40.598773]},"properties":{"id":169955,"url":"https://mycoast.org/reports/169955","date":"2022-10-02","place":"Arverne, Queens","hood":"Far Rockaway","boro":"Queens","text":"","img":"https://cdn.mycoast.photos/2024/06/01190749/3e1d08225546870de89d8086d16b2bef48023e48-scaled.jpg","depth":5,"flooded":"Roads/streets, Lawns/vegetation","rain24":0.847}},{"type":"Feature","geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-73.971345,40.645451]},"properties":{"id":169925,"url":"https://mycoast.org/reports/169925","date":"2022-09-13","place":"Kensington, Brooklyn","hood":"Kensington","boro":"Brooklyn","text":"The city sewer has backed up into the basements on my block again. Basements are flooded all over my neighborhood due to city sewer insufficiency. Kensington needs to be included in city plans to improve sewer system and add rain gardens.","img":"","depth":null,"flooded":"Lawns/vegetation","rain24":0.711}},{"type":"Feature","geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-73.881707,40.737946]},"properties":{"id":169936,"url":"https://mycoast.org/reports/169936","date":"2022-09-13","place":"Elmhurst","hood":"Elmhurst","boro":"Queens","text":"The flooding was caused by 2 things: a water main along the service road of Queens Blvd. westbound which was not fixed for 2 weeks previous to that so water was coming out from the roadway and a heavy rain storm which added to the burden that the existing catch basins were handling (the water from the water main break + the additional storm waters). The flooding was akin to Ida where water not only went over the curb but seeped into the vestibule of the nearby buildings.","img":"","depth":5,"flooded":"Roads/streets, Sidewalks, Lawns/vegetation","rain24":1.352}},{"type":"Feature","geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-73.859043,40.734446]},"properties":{"id":169961,"url":"https://mycoast.org/reports/169961","date":"2022-09-13","place":"Rego Park","hood":"Rego Park","boro":"Queens","text":"I live in Park City Estates in a ground floor unit. 5 ground floor units, including mine, flooded on September 13, 2022. The cooperative and the city have not done anything to fix recurring flooding issues.","img":"","depth":null,"flooded":"Roads/streets, Sidewalks, Parking lots, Lawns/vegetation","rain24":1.27}},{"type":"Feature","geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-73.973354,40.649455]},"properties":{"id":169923,"url":"https://mycoast.org/reports/169923","date":"2022-09-13","place":"Brooklyn","hood":"Windsor Terrace","boro":"Brooklyn","text":"","img":"","depth":4,"flooded":"Roads/streets, Sidewalks, Lawns/vegetation","rain24":0.721}},{"type":"Feature","geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-74.017621,40.620922]},"properties":{"id":169929,"url":"https://mycoast.org/reports/169929","date":"2022-09-13","place":"10th Avenue - Dyker Heights Brooklyn NY, 11228","hood":"Dyker Heights","boro":"Brooklyn","text":"sidewalks at corners under water and sewer back up into homes of everyone I spoke to including myself on the Avenue.   Most people got a few inches of water in their basements. It happens every time there is a powerful storm","img":"","depth":2,"flooded":"Sidewalks, Lawns/vegetation","rain24":0.521}},{"type":"Feature","geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-73.81708,40.608894]},"properties":{"id":169797,"url":"https://mycoast.org/reports/169797","date":"2022-01-02","place":"Broad channel","hood":"Broad Channel","boro":"Queens","text":"","img":"https://cdn.mycoast.photos/2024/06/01184429/15aa18cbf55e8776e394a3e9b6bdec8745c25f23-scaled.jpg","depth":null,"flooded":"Roads/streets, Sidewalks, Lawns/vegetation","rain24":1.186}},{"type":"Feature","geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-73.81702,40.608273]},"properties":{"id":169794,"url":"https://mycoast.org/reports/169794","date":"2022-01-02","place":"Broad Channel","hood":"Far Rockaway","boro":"Queens","text":"","img":"https://cdn.mycoast.photos/2024/06/01184336/3fe974fa7cf4ab7787494fb45c4654a6fed9f395-scaled.jpg","depth":20,"flooded":"Roads/streets, Sidewalks, Lawns/vegetation","rain24":1.185}},{"type":"Feature","geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-73.777905,40.710839]},"properties":{"id":120189,"url":"https://mycoast.org/reports/120189","date":"2021-09-01","place":"Hollis Queens","hood":"Jamaica","boro":"Queens","text":"183rd Street In Hollis Queens from Hurricane Ida.","img":"https://cdn.mycoast.photos/2023/06/21194127/20210901_221628-scaled.jpg","depth":66,"flooded":"Roads/streets, Sidewalks, Lawns/vegetation, Structures","rain24":1.221}},{"type":"Feature","geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-73.777992,40.711299]},"properties":{"id":120192,"url":"https://mycoast.org/reports/120192","date":"2021-09-01","place":"Hollis Queens","hood":"Jamaica","boro":"Queens","text":"90th Ave and 183rd Street Hollis Queens","img":"https://cdn.mycoast.photos/2023/06/21195159/20210901_221005-scaled.jpg","depth":55,"flooded":"Roads/streets, Sidewalks, Lawns/vegetation, Structures","rain24":1.222}},{"type":"Feature","geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-74.142662,40.570579]},"properties":{"id":169965,"url":"https://mycoast.org/reports/169965","date":"2021-09-01","place":"Staten Island","hood":"Richmond","boro":"Staten Island","text":"During Hurricane Ida on September 1, 2021, all of Ardsley Street was covered with 18 inches of water, and every house with a basement was completely flooded.  My basement is below street level, and was filled with 3 feet of water.  At the end of the Ardsley St is a large grassy area that is part of someone's backyard.  That grassy area filled with water from the heavy rain, and turned into a small lake.  Eventually it spilled over into the street, overwhelming the storm drains.  Adding a storm drain on that property might mitigate the problem entirely.","img":"https://cdn.mycoast.photos/2024/06/01190937/e1e2cfb5d430ba78b57dfa17887617e58e0141bd.jpg","depth":36,"flooded":"Roads/streets, Sidewalks, Parking lots, Lawns/vegetation","rain24":4.103}}]}